WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.320
from a strictly strategic perspective, Joe
Biden should pick Elizabeth.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.630
Warren, as his vice president, I'm going to
make the case for that now.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:15.599
Joe Biden already committed to choosing a
woman to be his running mate.

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:21.410
Joe Biden has been asked more and more lately
to select a woman of color.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:27.230
We saw Senator Amy Klobuchar remove her name
from consideration, saying Joe should really

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.560
pick a woman of color now.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:34.240
I think part of it was Amy Klobuchar was wrapped
up in the whole Derrick Schavan fiasco.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.620
We won't revisit that now, but I think that
played a role.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.600
But in any case, Amy Klobuchar dropping out
and saying Joe should really pick a woman

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.620
of color rather than me.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.710
And that would be powerful in its own way.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:50.219
But from a merely strategic point of view,
I believe Elizabeth Warren actually makes

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:51.520
the most sense.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:58.780
If you ballons name recognition, how progressive
the candidates being considered are and the

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:03.540
effect that the choice would have on the electorate
based on polling that we have.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.590
Elizabeth Warren seems like clearly the right
selection to me.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:13.049
Now, there's a lot of talk about Kamala Harris,
a black woman, current senator from California.

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:15.119
Harris's identity would be very powerful.

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:18.659
The first woman V.P. also being a black woman.

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:20.999
There's no doubt that would be very powerful.

00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:26.249
The problem is Kamala Harris is prosecutorial
record as attorney general in the state of

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:27.859
California.

00:01:27.859 --> 00:01:31.959
And that is not likely to pull in disaffected
Bernie voters.

00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:36.099
It's not likely to appeal to the progressive
wing of the Democratic Party.

00:01:36.099 --> 00:01:43.069
I don't believe that the disaffected Bernie
voters are like this huge portion of the electorate.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.430
But this could be a very close race, particularly
in some key states.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:54.509
And seeing a prosecutor of the failed war
on drugs being Joe Biden's V.P. will do more

00:01:54.509 --> 00:02:01.389
damage, I believe, than the benefit of Kamala
Harris is identity as a woman of color.

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:05.739
You then seem names seen names thrown around
like Stacey Abrams.

00:02:05.739 --> 00:02:07.399
Now, I like Stacey Abrams.

00:02:07.399 --> 00:02:09.439
She was a Georgia state rep.

00:02:09.439 --> 00:02:12.530
She ran for governor in Georgia in 2018.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:17.469
I don't believe she has the experience nor
the name recognition to really help Joe Biden

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:18.540
very much.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.651
I don't actually believe she's a top candidate
right now.

00:02:20.651 --> 00:02:23.599
I think there's a very small chance that she
is selected.

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:28.510
Joe Biden is also reportedly considering Val
Demings, a black congresswoman from Florida

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:31.519
and Michigan Governor Aggression Wittmer from
Michigan.

00:02:31.519 --> 00:02:34.790
And there's an interesting case to be made
for either of them.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:41.090
But it seems very clear to me that Elizabeth
Warren, after Bernie, is the next most progressive

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:46.189
candidate that was in the running in the Democratic
primary in 2020.

00:02:46.189 --> 00:02:51.260
And she has the name recognition and she has
some important accomplishments to her name,

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.709
including the Consumer Financial Protection
Bureau.

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:59.379
When you talk about structural reform and
you look at Kamala Harris versus Elizabeth

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:04.390
Warren, Warren is much closer to being the
structural change candidate than Harris.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.560
There's no doubt that Bernie was these structural
change candidate.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.849
No question about it.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:10.430
But after Bernie, it's Warren.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:11.430
It's not Harris.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.079
And I think that that will have an appeal
that the other candidates will not have to

00:03:15.079 --> 00:03:17.660
make this point a different way.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:22.349
Warren would mobilize the group that Biden
needs.

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:26.000
Biden has 92 percent support from black voters.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.239
Biden is not as strong with the most progressive
piece of the electorate.

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:34.110
That's who Warren helps the most with.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.519
And I don't think she hurts him with black
voters at all.

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:41.239
And in fact, there's a morning consult poll
that shows that Warren would bring in more

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:43.599
black voters than even Harris would.

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:47.670
And even then, Stacey Abrams would, which
are very, very interesting and and results

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:50.569
that reinforce Warren being the strongest
pick.

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:55.879
So, in short, to put it very simply, Warren
is the most progressive, highly known person

00:03:55.879 --> 00:03:57.629
being considered.

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:02.950
And in the polls, she helps Biden the most,
not only with the most progressive voters,

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.409
but also with black voters.

00:04:04.409 --> 00:04:05.920
So that's who I would go with.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:11.590
Now, that being said, there are all sorts
of ancillary reasons to focus in on a woman

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:13.390
of color instead of a white woman.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.769
I don't deny that for a second.

00:04:15.769 --> 00:04:21.699
There's also a case that Biden that Warren,
rather, would be a strong cabinet pick for

00:04:21.699 --> 00:04:27.060
Biden if she weren't V.P. and she could be
very strong as treasury secretary, secretary

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.639
of commerce, other possibilities.

00:04:29.639 --> 00:04:33.900
But vice president would be powerful and it
would make an impact right away.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.680
Biden is reportedly going to make his choice
around August 1st.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.229
So we will see who it is.

00:04:38.229 --> 00:04:42.199
One one just other argument against Elizabeth
Warren that I've seen, which is not a not

00:04:42.199 --> 00:04:47.430
a crazy one, is the argument that Warren is
more valuable in the Senate and that if she

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:53.639
leaves sometimes in Massachusetts in these
special elections, we elect Republicans to

00:04:53.639 --> 00:04:54.639
the Senate.

00:04:54.639 --> 00:04:56.250
We saw it with Scott Brown.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:00.310
This is not a seat we can afford to lose when
we are looking to take control of the Senate

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.340
in the fall.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.419
I don't know if it will happen.

00:05:02.419 --> 00:05:07.169
It's an uphill battle so that that would be
an argument against Elizabeth.

00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:10.759
But it would be great to watch her destroy
Mike Pence in those debates, wouldn't it?

00:05:10.759 --> 00:05:28.000
So my choice is Elizabeth Warren.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:47.810
I

00:05:47.810 --> 00:06:28.199
want to hear from you.

